{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
  "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As this case comes to the Court, two things I think are uncontested. The first is that at this trial, the prosecution suppressed all of the evidence in its files that went to the single most important contested issue of the case, and that's whether the defendant was a drug addict and committed the crimes in an amphetamine psychosis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is also a third thing that's uncontested, which is there is no Brady claim on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did that raise a discussion of the Brady claim on the merits, saying that the district court was wrong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it your view that the evidence was deliberately suppressed or negligently suppressed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Deliberately suppressed, although it doesn't matter under Brady. There was -- they turned over almost nothing, and this was the heart of our case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Smith",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that as a legal matter there was no -- no need to turn it over because it was immaterial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: That was not my question. Was it favorable evidence? Did it have a tendency to favor the defendant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If we read the -- can I ask you this: If we read the decision of the Court of Criminal Appeals as having ratified the -- the district court's -- the -- the lower court's treatment of the procedural default issues, having rejected it on the ground that it was previously decided, that would be an instance in which a State court applied a procedural default rule based on an undisputed error of fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On page 22 and 24a of the petition appendix, the court of appeals says the claim was procedurally defaulted because it was previously determined. That's wrong. That is the argument that was passed upon by the court of appeals, and that should be reversed on procedural grounds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Is there anything in the court of appeals' treatment of the Brady claim on the merits that suggests it also treated them separately in the different silos, as you put it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Where do they say that they're only considering the categories separately?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What was the photographic evidence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa3ebe7fb3b90e4a2b63bdc4a817bdd1554f0705874e58babafe0423b4b578cc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa3ebe7fb3b9-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
